  "initialize": {
    "instructions": "DesignCraft is a page-layout app (an InDesign clone). Coordinates are points in spread space (y down; on a single-page spread the page's top-left is (0,0); a default Letter page is 612\u00d7792). Every action is a command: find ids and parameters with list_commands and run them with execute (or several with batch). Typical flow: new_document \u2192 execute frame.create {rect:[x0,y0,x1,y1], content:\"text\", text:\"\u2026\"} \u2192 set_story_text / execute type.char / style.paragraph.apply \u2192 render_page to look at the result. inspect_document lists pages, items (ids, bounds), stories (overset) and styles. place_image puts a picture on the page. Backend: headless (in-process engine, no window). Community: https://discord.gg/artcraft (Discord), https://getartcraft.com/apps/designcraft (app page), https://github.com/storytold/designcraft (source). The `app.links` command returns these links.",
